---
description: Never annotate a function return as -> None
alwaysApply: true
---

# No `-> None` return annotations

Omit the return annotation when a function returns nothing. `-> None` is redundant.

```python
# ❌ BAD
def delete_previous_content(content_ids: List[int]) -> None:
    previous_content.delete()

# ✅ GOOD
def delete_previous_content(content_ids: List[int]):
    previous_content.delete()
```

Annotate a return only when the function returns a value.
